# Code owners for nooxy.
#
# The `protect_branches` ruleset sets require_code_owner_review: true. Without
# this file that rule is inert — GitHub asks for review from the owners of the
# files changed, and with no owners declared, every PR satisfies it vacuously.
# The rule reads as active in the settings UI while doing nothing.
#
# One line, not a list of paths. @draphy is currently the only account with
# write access, so every path-specific rule would name the same owner and add
# nothing but the chance of the catch-all and a path rule drifting apart. Split
# it by path when there is a second maintainer to split it between.
#
# Outside contributors are deliberately not listed. A CODEOWNERS entry for an
# account without write access is silently ignored by GitHub, so adding one
# would look like coverage while providing none.
#
# Note this repository is user-owned rather than an organisation, so team
# syntax (@org/team) is not available here — owners must be individual users.

* @draphy
